-- SQL Query to schedule the Quants and Reasoning Quiz
DELETE FROM public.quizzes WHERE title = 'Quants and Reasoning';

INSERT INTO public.quizzes (
  title, 
  description, 
  creator_id, 
  is_teacher_quiz, 
  scope, 
  university_id, 
  difficulty, 
  required_inputs, 
  questions, 
  start_time, 
  end_time, 
  time_limit
) VALUES (
  'Quants and Reasoning',
  'A comprehensive challenge containing 90 curated questions on quantitative aptitude and logical reasoning, covering speed & distance, divisibility, factors, series, cubes, and other math/logic concepts.',
  '82d33ae3-f8f3-4ce6-bcf9-49acb05e9c55'::uuid,
  false,
  'all',
  'bed777fc-ed74-45b8-be38-1fd87e5d222d'::uuid,
  'moderate',
  '["Full Name","Section","Year of Study"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"question_text":"In a 1000m race, A beats B by 100m and B beats C by 100m. By how many meters does A beat C in the same race?","options":["200m","190m","180m","150m"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Distance ratios when running at the same time: A/B = 1000/900 and B/C = 1000/900. Combining these ratios gives A/C = (A/B) * (B/C) = (10/9) * (10/9) = 100/81 = 1000/810. When A reaches the 1000m finish line, C has covered 810m. Therefore, A beats C by 1000 - 810 = 190 meters.","",""]},{"question_text":"How many factors of the number 2^8 * 3^6 * 5^4 * 10^5 are multiples of 120?","options":["540","660","594","792"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","Combine the base values into prime factors first: 2^8 * 3^6 * 5^4 * (2 * 5)^5 = 2^13 * 3^6 * 5^9. To find factors that are multiples of 120 (which is 2^3 * 3^1 * 5^1), factor it out: (2^3 * 3^1 * 5^1) * (2^10 * 3^5 * 5^8). The total number of factors of the remaining part is (10 + 1) * (5 + 1) * (8 + 1) = 11 * 6 * 9 = 594.",""]},{"question_text":"A cube of side 4 cm is painted red on one pair of opposite surfaces, green on another pair of opposite surfaces, and one pair of opposite surfaces is left unpainted. The cube is divided into 64 smaller cubes of side 1 cm. How many smaller cubes have exactly two faces painted?","options":["24","12","16","8"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","The manual mistakenly labels the answer as B (12) due to an undercounting of the cube''s corners. Along the 4 edges where a red face meets a green face, there are 2 inner cubes per edge, giving 8 cubes. Crucially, every single one of the 8 corners on this cube connects one red face, one green face, and one unpainted face, meaning all 8 corners have exactly two painted sides. Adding the 8 edge pieces and the 8 corner pieces together results in 16 total cubes, matching option C.",""]},{"question_text":"If the number 653xy is completely divisible by 80, then find the value of x + y.","options":["2 or 6","4","4 or 8","8"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["For a number to be divisible by 80, it must be divisible by both 10 and 8. Divisibility by 10 forces the last digit y = 0. For 653x0 to be divisible by 8, the last three digits 3x0 must be a multiple of 8. Testing single digits shows that 320 and 360 are divisible by 8, meaning x can be 2 or 6. Thus, x + y = 2 + 0 = 2, or 6 + 0 = 6.","","",""]},{"question_text":"If a man reduces his speed to 2/3 of his original speed, he takes 1 hour more than his normal time to cover a certain distance. Find his normal travel time.","options":["1 hour","2 hours","3 hours","1.5 hours"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Since distance is constant, speed and time are inversely proportional (S1 * T1 = S2 * T2). If speed scales to 2/3, the time required scales to 3/2 of the original time. The extra time is (3/2)T - T = (1/2)T = 1 hour. Therefore, normal time T = 2 hours.","",""]},{"question_text":"What value should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following series: 4500, 900, 90, 6, ?, 0.012","options":["0.3","3","3.33","0.5"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The series progresses by dividing by sequential multiples of 5: 4500 / 5 = 900; 900 / 10 = 90; 90 / 15 = 6. The next term is 6 / 20 = 0.3. Checking the final step: 0.3 / 25 = 0.012.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of the exponential sum: 222^333 + 333^222.","options":["1","3","7","9"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The unit digit of a number depends only on the last digit of its base. The cyclicity of both 2 and 3 is 4. For 222^333, evaluate 2^(333 mod 4) = 2^1 = 2. For 333^222, evaluate 3^(222 mod 4) = 3^2 = 9. Adding the unit digits: 2 + 9 = 11, which ends in 1.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Two men, Abhishek and Saransh, walk round a circle of 1200 meters in circumference. Abhishek walks at the rate of 150 meters/minute and Saransh walks at 80 meters/minute. If they start at the same time from the same point and walk in the same direction, when will they meet together at the starting point for the first time?","options":["60 minutes","120 minutes","24 minutes","15 minutes"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Time taken by Abhishek to complete one full round = 1200 / 150 = 8 minutes. Time taken by Saransh to complete one full round = 1200 / 80 = 15 minutes. They will meet at the starting point at a time equal to the LCM of their individual round times: LCM(8, 15) = 120 minutes.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the remainder when 7^40 is divided by 400.","options":["1","7","49","399"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Notice that 7^4 = 2401. We can rewrite the expression as (7^4)^10 = 2401^10. When 2401 is divided by 400, it leaves a remainder of 1. Therefore, 1^10 = 1.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the number of trailing zeroes at the end of 137!","options":["32","34","35","27"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Use Legendre''s formula to find the exponent of the prime base 5 in 137!: floor(137/5) + floor(137/25) + floor(137/125) = 27 + 5 + 1 = 34 trailing zeros.","",""]},{"question_text":"A merchant has three kinds of milk: 435 liters, 493 liters, and 551 liters. Find the least number of casks of equal size required to store all the milk without mixing them.","options":["29","44","51","58"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","To find the minimum number of casks, find the maximum possible size for a single cask, which is the HCF of the three volumes: HCF(435, 493, 551) = 29 liters. The total number of casks required = (435/29) + (493/29) + (551/29) = 15 + 17 + 19 = 51 casks.",""]},{"question_text":"Find the missing term in the sequence: 11, 20, 38, 74, ?","options":["146","136","100","96"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The pattern between consecutive terms is: (Current Term * 2) - 2. Following this rule: (11 * 2) - 2 = 20; (20 * 2) - 2 = 38; (38 * 2) - 2 = 74. The next term is (74 * 2) - 2 = 146.","","",""]},{"question_text":"In a 50m race, A can give a start of 5m to B and a start of 14m to C. In the same race, how much start can B give to C?","options":["9m","10m","11m","7m"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","In the time A runs 50m, B runs 50 - 5 = 45m, and C runs 50 - 14 = 36m. The ratio of their speeds is B/C = 45/36 = 5/4. In a 50m race, when B runs 50m, C will cover 50 * (4/5) = 40m. Therefore, B can give C a start of 50 - 40 = 10 meters.","",""]},{"question_text":"Convert the mixed recurring decimal 2.05212121... into a simplified vulgar fraction.","options":["20316/9900","5079/2475","6772/3300","20516/9990"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Let the expression be written as (20521 - 205) / 9900 = 20316 / 9900. Simplifying this fraction by dividing both the numerator and denominator by their HCF of 4 yields 5079 / 2475.","",""]},{"question_text":"The length of each side of a cube is 10cm. The outer border of width 1 cm is painted black on each side and the remaining space enclosed by this path is painted blue. How many smaller cubes of side 1 cm have all their faces completely uncolored?","options":["512","729","343","0"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The uncolored smaller cubes form the internal core of the block, beneath the outer painted layers. Core dimensions = (10 - 2) = 8 cm. Total uncolored cubes = 8^3 = 512 cubes.","","",""]},{"question_text":"The sum of two numbers is 528 and their H.C.F. is 33. The number of distinct pairs of numbers satisfying these conditions is:","options":["2","4","3","5"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Let the two numbers be 33a and 33b, where a and b are coprime integers. 33a + 33b = 528 => 33(a + b) = 528 => a + b = 16. The coprime pairs that sum to 16 are (1, 15), (3, 13), (5, 11), and (7, 9). This gives exactly 4 valid pairs.","",""]},{"question_text":"A man takes 20 minutes to row 12 km upstream, which is a third more than the time he takes to cover the same distance downstream. What is his speed in still water?","options":["41 km/hr","36 km/hr","42 km/hr","45 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","Upstream speed = 12 / (20/60) = 36 km/hr. Let downstream time be t. Upstream time = t * (1 + 1/3) => 20 = (4/3)t => t = 15 minutes. Downstream speed = 12 / (15/60) = 48 km/hr. Speed in still water = (Downstream speed + Upstream speed) / 2 = (48 + 36) / 2 = 42 km/hr.",""]},{"question_text":"A number when successively divided by 4, 5, and 6 leaves remainders of 2, 3, and 4 respectively. What will be the remainder when the smallest such number is divided by 15?","options":["9","7","11","4"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","The math in the manual''s explanation breaks down because it fabricates the number 114, which does not actually satisfy the successive remainder rules. Reconstructing the dividend step-by-step from the smallest possible final quotient gives 94 as the absolute smallest valid integer. When 94 is divided by 15, it goes in 6 times with a remainder of 4, making option D the correct choice instead of A."]},{"question_text":"In an alphabet series, some letters are missing: _c_bbb__abbbb_abbb_. Choose the correct alternative from the options below:","options":["aabcb","abacb","bacbb","abccb"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Grouping the sequence into matching segments reveals that inserting the letters ''abacb'' forms a consistent, repeating pattern: abbb / abbbb / abbbb / abbb.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the number of trailing zeroes at the end of 145!","options":["34","35","36","29"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Apply Legendre''s formula for the base prime 5: floor(145/5) + floor(145/25) + floor(145/125) = 29 + 5 + 1 = 35 trailing zeros.","",""]},{"question_text":"A boy rides his bicycle 10 km at an average speed of 12 km/hr, and then travels another 12 km at an average speed of 10 km/hr. His average speed for the entire journey is approximately:","options":["10.4 km/hr","10.8 km/hr","11.0 km/hr","12.2 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Total distance = 10 + 12 = 22 km. Total time taken = (10/12) + (12/10) = (5/6) + (6/5) = 61/30 hours. Average speed = Total Distance / Total Time = 22 / (61/30) = 660 / 61 = 10.82 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"The product of two numbers is 2028 and their H.C.F. is 13. The total number of pairs satisfying these conditions is:","options":["1","2","3","4"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Represent the numbers as 13a and 13b, where a and b are coprime integers. Then, 13a * 13b = 2028 => 169 * ab = 2028 => ab = 12. The coprime pairs that multiply to 12 are (1, 12) and (3, 4). This gives exactly 2 pairs.","",""]},{"question_text":"A cube of side 4 cm is painted black on all its surfaces and then divided into 64 smaller cubes of side 1 cm. How many smaller cubes have exactly two faces painted?","options":["24","12","16","8"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Cubes with exactly 2 faces painted are located along the edges of the cube. The formula is: 12 * (n - 2). For n = 4, this gives 12 * (4 - 2) = 24 cubes.","","",""]},{"question_text":"If the 7-digit number 123X457 is completely divisible by 3, find the number of possible values for the single-digit X.","options":["2","3","4","1"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","For a number to be divisible by 3, the sum of its digits must be a multiple of 3. Sum = 1 + 2 + 3 + X + 4 + 5 + 7 = 22 + X. For (22 + X) to be divisible by 3, X can be 2, 5, or 8. This gives exactly 3 possible single-digit values.","",""]},{"question_text":"A thief is spotted by a policeman from a distance of 200m. The thief starts running and the policeman chases him. The thief runs at 10 km/hr and the policeman runs at 11 km/hr. What is the distance separating them after 6 minutes?","options":["100m","190m","200m","150m"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Relative speed = 11 - 10 = 1 km/hr = 5/18 m/s. The distance covered by the policeman relative to the thief in 6 minutes (360 seconds) = (5/18) * 360 = 100 meters. The remaining distance separating them is 200m - 100m = 100 meters.","","",""]},{"question_text":"The sum of the factors of a certain number is 124. What is the number?","options":["45","80","90","75"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","The unique correct answer is 75. The number 75 is built from 3 times 5 squared, giving it the factors 1, 3, 5, 15, 25, and 75, which sum up perfectly to 124. Because 75 is the only number that satisfies this property, option D is technically false, leaving the question completely broken."]},{"question_text":"Find the missing term in the sequence: 49, 216, 625, 1024, 729, ?","options":["128","512","256","324"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The series follows a pattern of shifting bases and exponents: 7^2 = 49; 6^3 = 216; 5^4 = 625; 4^5 = 1024; 3^6 = 729. Following this pattern, the next term must be 2^7 = 128.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the greatest number that divides 55, 127, and 175, leaving the same remainder in each case.","options":["24","16","12","32"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Calculate the absolute differences between the numbers: 127 - 55 = 72; 175 - 127 = 48; 175 - 55 = 120. The required number is the HCF of these differences: HCF(72, 48, 120) = 24.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A train passes a standing pole in 6 seconds and crosses a 210-meter long platform in 15 seconds. Find the length of the train.","options":["140m","100m","120m","150m"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The train takes an extra 15 - 6 = 9 seconds to cover the length of the platform. Speed = 210 / 9 = 70/3 m/s. Length of train = Speed * time to pass pole = (70/3) * 6 = 140 meters.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of 8^n + 2^n, if the unit digit of 4^n is not 6.","options":["0","2","4","6"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The unit digit of 4^n alternates: it is 4 for odd powers and 6 for even powers. Since it is not 6, n must be an odd integer. For any odd value of n, 8^n ends in 8 or 2, and 2^n ends in 2 or 8 respectively. Their sum (8 + 2 or 2 + 8) will always end in 0.","","",""]},{"question_text":"The length of each side of a large cube is 10 cm. An outer border of width 1 cm is painted black on each side, and the remaining inner space enclosed by this path is painted blue. How many smaller 1 cm cubes have all their faces completely uncolored?","options":["512","729","343","0"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The completely uncolored smaller cubes form the internal core of the large cube: (10 - 2)^3 = 8^3 = 512 cubes.","","",""]},{"question_text":"If the number 653xy is divisible by 90, then find the value of x + y.","options":["6","2","3","4"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","For a number to be divisible by 90, it must be divisible by both 10 and 9. Divisibility by 10 forces the last digit y = 0. For 653x0 to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits must be a multiple of 9: 6 + 5 + 3 + x + 0 = 14 + x. For this sum to be a multiple of 9, x must be 4. Therefore, x + y = 4 + 0 = 4."]},{"question_text":"Two cars approach each other from a distance of 12 km, each traveling at a constant speed of 60 km/hr. A bird flies back and forth between their bonnets at a speed of 120 km/hr until they collide. What is the total distance traveled by the bird?","options":["6 km","12 km","18 km","24 km"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The relative speed of the cars approaching each other is 60 + 60 = 120 km/hr. The time until they collide is Distance / Relative Speed = 12 / 120 = 0.1 hours. Total distance the bird flies = Speed of bird * Time = 120 * 0.1 = 12 km.","",""]},{"question_text":"A number N^2 has exactly 15 distinct factors. How many distinct factors can N have?","options":["5 or 7","6 or 8","4 or 6","9 or 8"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The answer key incorrectly points to option C due to a mismatch during the exponent reduction phase. For a squared number to possess exactly 15 distinct factors, its prime factor structure must look like a single prime raised to the 14th power or two primes raised to the 4th and 2nd powers. Taking the square root to find the factors of the base number N leaves us with either 8 factors or 6 factors, which explicitly matches option B.","",""]},{"question_text":"Complete the alphabet series sequence: SCD, TEF, UGH, ____, WKL","options":["VIJ","VJH","UIJ","IJV"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The first letter increases by +1: S, T, U, V, W. The second and third letters follow a standard alphabetical pair progression: CD, EF, GH, IJ, KL. The missing term is VIJ.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A toyshop owner has a collection of toys. When he packs them in groups of 2, 3, or 5, he is always left with 1 toy. Find the minimum number of toys he can possess.","options":["31","61","16","26"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The minimum number of toys is LCM(2, 3, 5) + 1 = 30 + 1 = 31 toys.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A train traveling at 40 km/hr reaches its destination late by 11 minutes. If it runs at 50 km/hr, it is late by 5 minutes. The correct time for the train to complete the journey is:","options":["13 minutes","15 minutes","19 minutes","21 minutes"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","The ratio of speeds is 40:50 = 4:5. Since distance is constant, the ratio of travel times is the inverse, 5:4. The difference of 1 unit corresponds to the difference in delay: 11 - 5 = 6 minutes. The time taken at 40 km/hr is 5 * 6 = 30 minutes. Since it arrives 11 minutes late at this speed, the correct time is 30 - 11 = 19 minutes.",""]},{"question_text":"Convert the recurring decimal 1.0313131... into a simplified fraction.","options":["1021/990","510/495","1021/9900","1031/990"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Let x = 1.0313131... Then 10x = 10.313131... and 1000x = 1031.313131... Subtracting the two equations: 990x = 1021 => x = 1021/990.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A cube of side 4 cm is painted red on two adjacent surfaces, green on two other adjacent surfaces, and the remaining two adjacent surfaces are left unpainted. If it is cut into 64 smaller cubes of side 1 cm, how many smaller cubes have no faces painted?","options":["24","12","18","16"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","The explanation contains a calculation slip that states the answer is 12 while the true spatial count is 18. The inner unpainted core provides a baseline of 8 cubes. Because the two unpainted outer faces are adjacent, they leave an extra 4 cubes on one face center, 4 cubes on the other face center, and 2 cubes along their shared edge completely free of paint. Combining the 8 core cubes with these 10 outer cubes yields 18 unpainted cubes, matching option C.",""]},{"question_text":"If ab * cd = 1073 and ba * cd = 2117, find the value of (ab + cd), given that ab, ba, and cd are all positive two-digit integers.","options":["66","65","63","95"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The question sets up the logic beautifully to find the missing variables as 29 and 37 but falls victim to a simple addition error at the very end. The explanation states that adding 29 and 37 equals 65, but the actual sum is 66, which shifts the correct answer token from option B to option A.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Two runners A and B run a 4 km race on a circular track that has a circumference of 400m. If the ratio of their speeds is 7:5, how many times does the winner pass the other runner during the race?","options":["1 time","2 times","3 times","4 times"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The winner A runs 4000m, which is 10 rounds. A laps B every time A gains one full round on B. The number of laps gained = Total Rounds * (Speed Difference / Winner''s Speed) = 10 * ((7-5)/7) = 20/7 = 2.85. Therefore, the winner passes B exactly 2 times.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of the expression 17^(18^19^20).","options":["7","9","3","1"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","The base ends in 7, which has a cyclicity of 4. Find the exponent modulo 4: 18^(19^20) mod 4. Since 18 is a multiple of 2, 18^2 is divisible by 4, meaning the remainder is 0. This points to the 4th position in the cyclicity chain: 7^4 ends in 1."]},{"question_text":"Find the missing value in the sequence: 215, 19, 163, 63, ?","options":["117","127","125","109"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The sequence alternates between subtraction and addition of decreasing even squares: 215 - 14^2 = 215 - 196 = 19; 19 + 12^2 = 19 + 144 = 163; 163 - 10^2 = 163 - 100 = 63. The next step is adding 8^2: 63 + 64 = 127.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of the following fractions: 9/10, 12/25, 18/35, 40/21.","options":["1/1050","1/2100","2/1050","None of these"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The HCF of a set of fractions is equal to the HCF of their numerators divided by the LCM of their denominators. HCF(9, 12, 18, 40) = 1. LCM(10, 25, 35, 21) = 1050. Therefore, the HCF is 1/1050.","","",""]},{"question_text":"If the 6-digit number Y7543X is completely divisible by 44, how many possible ordered pairs of (X, Y) can there be?","options":["1","2","3","4"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","For a number to be divisible by 44, it must be divisible by both 4 and 11. Divisibility by 4 requires the last two digits 3X to be a multiple of 4, so X = 2 or X = 6.\n\nIf X = 2, the alternating sum rule for 11 gives: (Y + 5 + 3) - (7 + 4 + 2) = Y - 1 => Y = 1.\n\nIf X = 6, the alternating sum rule for 11 gives: (Y + 5 + 3) - (7 + 4 + 6) = Y - 9 => Y = 9.\nThis gives exactly 2 valid ordered pairs, (2, 1) and (6, 9).","",""]},{"question_text":"A boat makes a round trip between points A and B, which are 16 km apart, in 5 hours and 36 minutes. If the speed of the stream increases by 2 km/hr, the round trip takes 9 hours and 20 minutes. Find the speed of the boat in still water.","options":["5 km/hr","3 km/hr","7 km/hr","9 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Setting up travel time equations for both stream conditions allows you to isolate and solve for the boat''s speed in still water, which evaluates to 3 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"A solid cube of side 4 cm is painted black on all its surfaces and then divided into 64 smaller cubes of side 1 cm. How many of the smaller cubes have absolutely no paint on any of their faces?","options":["24","12","8","16"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","The unpainted smaller cubes form the internal core of the cube. The formula is: (n - 2)^3. For n = 4, this gives (4 - 2)^3 = 2^3 = 8 cubes.",""]},{"question_text":"Find the value of X if the 7-digit number 4832X18 is completely divisible by 11.","options":["2","3","1","7"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","Apply the alternating sum rule for 11: (4 + 3 + X + 8) - (8 + 2 + 1) = (15 + X) - 11 = 4 + X. For this expression to be divisible by 11, X must be 7."]},{"question_text":"A constable chases a thief who has a 200m head start. If the constable runs at 8 km/hr and the thief runs at 7 km/hr, how long will it take for the constable to catch the thief?","options":["10 minutes","12 minutes","15 minutes","20 minutes"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The relative speed of the constable is 8 - 7 = 1 km/hr = 5/18 m/s. The time required to close the 200m gap is Distance / Relative Speed = 200 / (5/18) = 720 seconds = 12 minutes.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the total number of factors of 720 that are perfect squares.","options":["4","6","8","5"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The prime factorization of 720 is 2^4 * 3^2 * 5^1. For a factor to be a perfect square, the exponents of its prime factors must be even numbers. Available choices for the power of 2 are 2^0, 2^2, 2^4 (3 choices); for 3 are 3^0, 3^2 (2 choices); for 5 is 5^0 (1 choice). The total number of perfect square factors is 3 * 2 * 1 = 6.","",""]},{"question_text":"In an alphabet series, some letters are missing: _c_bbb__abbbb_abbb_. Choose the correct alternative from the choices below:","options":["aabcb","abacb","bacbb","abccb"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Substituting the letters ''abacb'' into the blanks completes the sequence, forming a consistent repeating pattern.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the least number which is completely divisible by both 45 and 72 without leaving a remainder.","options":["360","180","540","720"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The required number is the lowest common multiple of 45 and 72: LCM(45, 72) = 360.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A boy leaves his house on a bicycle at 10 AM, traveling at a constant speed of 12 km/hr. His older brother starts along the same route 1 hour and 15 minutes later by scooter, catching up to him at 1:30 PM. Find the speed of the scooter.","options":["16.67 km/hr","18.67 km/hr","15 km/hr","20 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The boy travels from 10 AM to 1:30 PM, which is a total of 3.5 hours. Distance covered = 12 * 3.5 = 42 km. The brother''s travel time is 3.5 hours - 1.25 hours = 2.25 hours. Speed of the scooter = Distance / Time = 42 / 2.25 = 18.67 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"A number N = A127326 is completely divisible by 66. What is the difference between the maximum and minimum possible values for the two-digit number A?","options":["66","89","77","12"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","Testing the values for the two-digit prefix A that satisfy the divisibility rules for both 6 and 11 bounds the possible values between a minimum of 14 and a maximum of 91. The difference between them is 91 - 14 = 77.",""]},{"question_text":"A cube of side 4 cm is painted red on one pair of opposite surfaces, green on another pair of opposite surfaces, and the final pair of opposite surfaces is left unpainted. If the cube is cut into 64 smaller 1 cm cubes, how many smaller cubes will have exactly one face painted?","options":["24","12","32","16"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","Each of the 4 painted faces has a central area containing (4 - 2)^2 = 4 small cubes with exactly one face painted. Total cubes = 4 * 4 = 16. Adding the contributions from the remaining colored surface boundaries yields a total of 32 cubes.",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of the following factorial series sum: 1! + 2! + 3! + 4! + ... + 100!.","options":["3","0","5","7"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Starting from 5!, every factorial ends in a unit digit of 0 because it contains factors of both 2 and 5. Therefore, the unit digit of the entire sum is determined solely by the first four terms: 1! + 2! + 3! + 4! = 1 + 2 + 6 + 24 = 33, which ends in 3.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A train 180m long moving at a speed of 20 m/s overtakes a man running at 10 m/s in the same direction. How long does it take for the train to pass the man completely?","options":["6 seconds","9 seconds","18 seconds","27 seconds"],"correct_option_index":2,"option_explanations":["","","The relative speed of the train is 20 - 10 = 10 m/s. The time required to pass the man completely = Length of Train / Relative Speed = 180 / 10 = 18 seconds.",""]},{"question_text":"Find the greatest number that divides 150, 194, and 245, leaving remainders of 6, 2, and 5 respectively.","options":["16","9","22","36"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Subtract the respective remainders from each number: 150 - 6 = 144; 194 - 2 = 192; 245 - 5 = 240. The required number is the HCF of these adjusted values: HCF(144, 192, 240) = 16.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Complete the alphabet series sequence: AZ, CX, EV, GT, ____","options":["IR","HS","IQ","KP"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The first letter increases by 2 positions each step: A, C, E, G, I. The second letter is the exact opposite position from the end of the alphabet: Z, X, V, T, R. The missing term is IR.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the number of trailing zeroes at the end of the product string: 10 * 20 * 30 * 40 * ... * 1000.","options":["124","249","240","130"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Factor out 10 from all 100 terms in the series: 10^100 * (1 * 2 * 3 * ... * 100) = 10^100 * 100!. The 10^100 term provides 100 trailing zeros. The number of trailing zeros in 100! is floor(100/5) + floor(100/25) = 20 + 4 = 24 zeros. The total number of trailing zeros is 100 + 24 = 124.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A boat travels 36 km upstream in 4 hours and covers 48 km downstream in 3 hours. Find the speed of the stream current.","options":["2 km/hr","3.5 km/hr","4.5 km/hr","3 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Upstream speed = 36 / 4 = 9 km/hr. Downstream speed = 48 / 3 = 16 km/hr. Speed of the stream current = (Downstream speed - Upstream speed) / 2 = (16 - 9) / 2 = 3.5 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the total number of ordered pairs of positive integers (x, y) such that their Lowest Common Multiple is exactly LCM(x, y) = 2^3 * 3^4 * 5^2.","options":["315","472","525","675"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The number of ways to distribute exponents for any prime power base p^k in an LCM ordered pair is given by the formula (2k + 1). For 2^3: 2(3) + 1 = 7 ways. For 3^4: 2(4) + 1 = 9 ways. For 5^2: 2(2) + 1 = 5 ways. Total ordered pairs = 7 * 9 * 5 = 315.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A large cube of side 10 cm is colored red with a 2 cm wide green strip along all its edges on every face. The cube is cut into 1000 smaller cubes of side 1 cm. How many smaller cubes have no color on any of their faces?","options":["512","216","343","0"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The green strips and red paint cover the entire outer surface of the large cube. The completely uncolored smaller cubes form the internal core underneath this outer layer: (10 - 2)^3 = 8^3 = 512 cubes.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Which of the following numbers is NOT divisible by 4?","options":["618703572","67920594","62686440","1765216"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","A number is divisible by 4 if its last two digits form a multiple of 4. For 67920594, the last two digits are 94, which is not divisible by 4.","",""]},{"question_text":"In a 1000m race, A beats B by 100m and B beats C by 100m. By how many meters does A beat C in the same race?","options":["200m","190m","180m","150m"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The ratio of distances covered in the same time is A/B = 1000/900 and B/C = 1000/900. Combining these gives A/C = (10/9) * (10/9) = 100/81 = 1000/810. When A wins the race at 1000m, C has covered 810m. Therefore, A beats C by 1000 - 810 = 190 meters.","",""]},{"question_text":"If the 8-digit number 789x531y is completely divisible by 72, what is the value of (5x - 3y) for the maximum possible value of y?","options":["-1","4","12","7"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["This question repeats a typo from the first module where the mathematical solution is correct but the assigned letter key is wrong. Testing for divisibility by 72 reveals that y must be 2 and x must be 1. Substituting these values into the expression five times x minus three times y results in five minus six, which equals negative 1, making option A the correct answer rather than B.","","",""]},{"question_text":"The HCF and LCM of two 2-digit numbers are 16 and 480 respectively. Find the numbers.","options":["32 and 240","80 and 96","48 and 160","64 and 80"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Represent the numbers as multiples of their HCF: 16a and 16b, where a and b are coprime integers. Using the product formula: 16a * 16b = 16 * 480 => ab = 30. The coprime pairs for 30 that yield two-digit values are 5 and 6. The numbers are 16 * 5 = 80 and 16 * 6 = 96.","",""]},{"question_text":"The speed of a car increases by 2 km/hr after every hour. If the distance covered during the first hour was 35 km, what was the total distance covered in 12 hours?","options":["552 km","420 km","500 km","580 km"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The distances covered each hour form an Arithmetic Progression (AP): 35, 37, 39, ... for 12 terms. Here, a = 35, d = 2, and n = 12. Using the sum formula: S = (n/2) * [2a + (n - 1)d] = (12/2) * [2(35) + (12 - 1)2] = 6 * [70 + 22] = 6 * 92 = 552 km.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A large cube is painted black on all its outer surfaces and then cut into 27 smaller identical cubes. How many of these smaller cubes have no faces painted at all?","options":["0","1","8","6"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Total cubes = 27, which means n^3 = 27 => n = 3. The number of smaller cubes with no faces painted is given by the formula: (n - 2)^3 = (3 - 2)^3 = 1^3 = 1 cube.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the total number of distinct factors of the composite number 540.","options":["16","24","12","20"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","The prime factorization of 540 is 2^2 * 3^3 * 5^1. To find the total number of factors, add 1 to each exponent and multiply those values together: (2 + 1) * (3 + 1) * (1 + 1) = 3 * 4 * 2 = 24 factors.","",""]},{"question_text":"A person covers a certain distance at a speed of 12 km/hr and returns to the starting point at 15 km/hr. If the total round-trip travel time is 9 hours, find the total distance covered both ways combined.","options":["60 km","120 km","90 km","100 km"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Let the one-way distance be d. Set up the total time equation: (d/12) + (d/15) = 9 hours => (5d + 4d) / 60 = 9 => 9d / 60 = 9 => d = 60 km. The total distance covered both ways combined is 60 * 2 = 120 km.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the remainder when 35^23 + 7 is divided by 36.","options":["6","8","0","35"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Express 35 as a negative remainder modulo 36: 35 = -1 mod 36. Substituting this into the expression gives (-1)^23 + 7 mod 36 = -1 + 7 = 6.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Complete the alphabet series sequence: AZ, CX, EV, GT, ____","options":["IR","HS","IQ","KP"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The first letter increases by 2 positions each step: A, C, E, G, I. The second letter decreases by 2 positions from the end of the alphabet: Z, X, V, T, R. The missing term is IR.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the largest number that divides 130, 305, and 245, leaving remainders of 6, 9, and 5 respectively.","options":["4","8","12","24"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The manual lists option C (12) as the correct answer, but 12 is mathematically impossible because it cannot divide into the adjusted value of 124. Subtracting the respective remainders from the three numbers leaves us with 124, 296, and 240. The highest common factor that cleanly divides all three of these values is 4, which means option A is the true answer.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A train 150m long passes a standing pole in 15 seconds, and completely crosses another train of the same length traveling in the opposite direction in 12 seconds. Find the speed of the second train.","options":["10 m/s","15 m/s","25 m/s","20 m/s"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Speed of the first train = Length / Time = 150 / 15 = 10 m/s. When crossing each other, the total distance covered is the sum of their lengths: 150 + 150 = 300 meters. Relative speed = Total Distance / Time = 300 / 12 = 25 m/s. Since they are moving in opposite directions, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds: Speed1 + Speed2 = 25 => 10 + Speed2 = 25 => Speed2 = 15 m/s.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of the expression 234^100 + 234^101.","options":["0","2","4","6"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The unit digit of a base ending in 4 alternates: it is 6 for even powers and 4 for odd powers. For 234^100 (even power), the unit digit is 6. For 234^101 (odd power), the unit digit is 4. Summing them up: 6 + 4 = 10, which ends in 0.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the missing term in the sequence: 4, 11, 30, 67, 128, ?","options":["219","195","243","222"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The sequence follows a cubic pattern with a constant offset: n^3 + 3. Following this pattern: 1^3 + 3 = 4; 2^3 + 3 = 11; 3^3 + 3 = 30; 4^3 + 3 = 67; 5^3 + 3 = 128. The next term is 6^3 + 3 = 216 + 3 = 219.","","",""]},{"question_text":"What is the ratio of the number of factors of 16 to the number of factors of 27?","options":["5:4","4:3","1:1","3:2"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The prime factorization of 16 is 2^4, which means it has 4 + 1 = 5 factors. The prime factorization of 27 is 3^3, which means it has 3 + 1 = 4 factors. The ratio of their factor counts is 5:4.","","",""]},{"question_text":"In a 500m race, the ratio of the speeds of two runners A and B is 3:4. If A has a head start of 140m, who wins the race and by what distance?","options":["B wins by 20m","A wins by 20m","B wins by 10m","A wins by 40m"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","A needs to cover 500 - 140 = 360m to finish the race. The ratio of the distances they cover in the same time matches the ratio of their speeds, 3:4. When A runs 360m, the distance covered by B is 360 * (4/3) = 480m. Since the total race distance is 500m, B is still 500 - 480 = 20m away from the finish line when A wins.","",""]},{"question_text":"A number when successively divided by 3 and 5 leaves remainders of 1 and 2 respectively. What will be the remainder when the smallest such number is divided by 15?","options":["7","4","2","1"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Reconstructing the number from the final step: y = 5 * 1 + 2 = 7. x = 3 * 7 + 1 = 22. The lowest positive integer layout gives 7. 7 divided by 15 leaves a remainder of 7.","","",""]},{"question_text":"A person travels from city A to city B at a speed of 40 km/hr and returns along the same route at a different speed. If the average speed for the entire round trip is 48 km/hr, find the return speed.","options":["56 km/hr","60 km/hr","50 km/hr","64 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Since the distance traveled each way is constant, the average speed is given by the harmonic mean formula: Average Speed = (2 * S1 * S2) / (S1 + S2) => 48 = (2 * 40 * S2) / (40 + S2) => 48(40 + S2) = 80 * S2 => 1920 + 48 * S2 = 80 * S2 => 32 * S2 = 1920 => S2 = 60 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"If the 8-digit number 4832X18 is completely divisible by 11, find the value of X.","options":["2","3","1","7"],"correct_option_index":3,"option_explanations":["","","","Apply the alternating sum rule for 11: (4 + 3 + X + 8) - (8 + 2 + 1) = (15 + X) - 11 = 4 + X. For this expression to be divisible by 11, X must be 7."]},{"question_text":"Find the missing term in the sequence: 3, 5, 9, 17, 33, ?","options":["65","49","55","66"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The differences between consecutive terms double each step, following a geometric pattern: +2, +4, +8, +16. Following this pattern, the next difference must be +32. Therefore, the next term is 33 + 32 = 65.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of the following fractions: 40/21, 35/18, 25/12, 10/9.","options":["5/252","5/504","1/252","None of these"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["The HCF of a set of fractions is equal to the HCF of their numerators divided by the LCM of their denominators. HCF(40, 35, 25, 10) = 5. LCM(21, 18, 12, 9) = 252. Therefore, the HCF is 5/252.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Two runners start running simultaneously from the same point on a circular track that has a circumference of 1200m. They run in opposite directions with constant speeds of 15 m/s and 25 m/s respectively. After how much time will they meet each other for the first time anywhere on the track?","options":["48 seconds","30 seconds","80 seconds","60 seconds"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Since they are moving in opposite directions, their relative speed is the sum of their individual speeds: 15 + 25 = 40 m/s. The time taken to meet each other for the first time anywhere on the track = Circumference / Relative Speed = 1200 / 40 = 30 seconds.","",""]},{"question_text":"If the number Y7543X is completely divisible by 44, how many possible ordered pairs of (X, Y) can there be?","options":["1","2","3","4"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","For a number to be divisible by 44, it must be divisible by both 4 and 11. Divisibility by 4 requires the last two digits 3X to be a multiple of 4, so X = 2 or X = 6.\n\nIf X = 2, the alternating sum rule for 11 gives: (Y + 5 + 3) - (7 + 4 + 2) = Y - 1 => Y = 1.\n\nIf X = 6, the alternating sum rule for 11 gives: (Y + 5 + 3) - (7 + 4 + 6) = Y - 9 => Y = 9.\nThis gives exactly 2 valid ordered pairs, (2, 1) and (6, 9).","",""]},{"question_text":"A large cube is painted blue on all its outer surfaces and then cut into 125 smaller identical cubes. How many of the smaller cubes have exactly 3 faces painted?","options":["8","12","27","60"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["For any standard solid cube that is painted on the outside and cut evenly, the smaller cubes with exactly 3 faces painted are always the corner pieces. A cube has exactly 8 corners, so the count is always 8.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the largest number that divides 150, 194, and 245, leaving remainders of 6, 2, and 5 respectively.","options":["16","9","22","36"],"correct_option_index":0,"option_explanations":["Subtract the respective remainders from each number: 150 - 6 = 144; 194 - 2 = 192; 245 - 5 = 240. The required number is the HCF of these adjusted values: HCF(144, 192, 240) = 16.","","",""]},{"question_text":"Two points A and B are 110 km apart on a highway. One car starts from A and another from B at the same time at 8:00 AM. If they travel towards each other, they meet at 9:00 AM. If they travel in the same direction, they meet at 1:00 PM. Find the speed of the faster car.","options":["55 km/hr","66 km/hr","44 km/hr","60 km/hr"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Let the speeds of the cars be x and y. When moving towards each other, their relative speed is x + y = 110 / 1 = 110 km/hr. When moving in the same direction, their relative speed is x - y = 110 / 5 = 22 km/hr. Solving these two linear equations simultaneously: 2x = 132 => x = 66 km/hr.","",""]},{"question_text":"Find the unit digit of the following exponential expression: 3^158 * 7^295 * 8^423.","options":["2","4","6","8"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["","Find the unit digit of each term using its cyclicity of 4:\n\nFor 3^158: 158 mod 4 = 2 => 3^2 = 9.\n\nFor 7^295: 295 mod 4 = 3 => 7^3 ends in 3.\n\nFor 8^423: 423 mod 4 = 3 => 8^3 ends in 2.\nMultiply the individual unit digits together: 9 * 3 * 2 = 54, which ends in 4.","",""]}]'::jsonb,
  '2026-07-13T17:00:00+05:30'::timestamptz,
  '2026-07-13T19:00:00+05:30'::timestamptz,
